/-
etcd's WAL over the per-byte Linux file extension (the part `LinuxFs/`: `wal`, `walpb`, `fileutil`
and the part's `os`, `syscall`, `ioutil`, `crc`, ... they call; `notes/wal-fsext-plan.md`, section
8, "Links"), every proof instantiated with its callees' results. The callees are read off each
proof's binders (`etc/link_walfs.py`'s docstring); a result is generic in the proof's model
parameters (`P`, `Mr`, ...). Generated by `etc/gen-link.py --walfs` -- do not edit by hand.

162 results, 119 of them with no hypothesis. The others take, as hypotheses `h_<name>`, the specs
with no proof and the premises on the model parameters (the client's protobuf laws, ...) they reach:
`h_U_Ok` (1), `h_U_SnapCoh` (1), `h_WalDecEnvSupply` (3), `h_WalHsOwn` (1), `h_WalPbIn_CloneHsLaw`
(1), `h_WalPbIn_GetIndexLaw` (3), `h_WalPbIn_GetTermLaw` (1), `h_WalPbIn_IsEmptyLaw` (3),
`h_WalPbIn_MarshalEntLaw` (2), `h_WalPbIn_MarshalHsLaw` (3), `h_WalPbIn_MustSyncLaw` (1),
`h_WalPbIn_UnmarshalEntLaw` (1), `h_WalPbIn_ZeroLaw` (1), `h_errors_AsLinkError` (1),
`h_errors_IsErrno` (5), `h_errors_IsPathErrnoEof` (3), `h_filepathlite_IsAbs` (8),
`h_fileutil_ReadDir` (8), `h_fileutil_ReadDirAbsentIs` (2), `h_fileutil_ReadDirChildIs` (2),
`h_fmt_ErrorfErrs` (18), `h_fmt_ErrorfErrsNot` (3), `h_fmt_ErrorfStrs` (3),
`h_proto_UnmarshalWalRecordE` (1), `h_wal_WAL_cut` (1), `h_wal_WAL_renameWALUnlock` (1),
`h_wal_WAL_sync` (4), `h_wal_WAL_syncC` (1), `h_wal_WAL_syncIdle` (2), `h_wal_WAL_syncPreL` (1),
`h_wal_closeAll` (4), `h_wal_decoder_Decode` (1), `h_wal_encoder_encodeG` (7).

`#print axioms` on a result is its trust base (`etc/tcb-report.py`).
-/
